# Architecture

```
app route → feature screen → query hook or Zustand store → API client or storage
```

## Routes

Files in `app/` re-export a screen or redirect. No `fetch`, Zod, or AsyncStorage there.

- `router.replace` for splash, login, and sign-out
- `router.push` for `/search` and `/movie/[id]`
- Search and detail sit on the root stack, not as extra tabs

## Features

- `src/features/movies` — schemas, TMDB API, query hooks, movie screens
- `src/features/session` — session store and login
- `src/features/settings` — theme store and settings
- `src/features/watchlist` and `watched` — persisted lists
- `src/features/recommendation` — Staff Pick
- `src/core` — env, theme, HTTP client, query client, shared UI

Screens do not call `fetch` or read AsyncStorage directly.

## Example

```tsx
// app/(app)/index.tsx
export { HomeScreen as default } from '@/src/features/movies/HomeScreen';
```
